'''Fabian Obmann''' (born 11 April 1996) is an Austrian [[Snowboarding|snowboarder]] specializing in parallel slalom and parallel giant slalom disciplines.

==Career==
Obmann competed at the [[FIS Freestyle Ski and Snowboarding World Championships 2023|2023 Snowboarding World Championships]] and finished in fourth place in the [[FIS Freestyle Ski and Snowboarding World Championships 2023 – Men's parallel slalom|parallel slalom]] event, losing to [[Arnaud Gaudet]] by .63 seconds during the small final.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.cbc.ca/sports/olympics/winter/snowboard/arnaud-gaudet-snowboard-parallal-slalom-bronze-bakuriani-1.6755575 |title=Canadian snowboarder Arnaud Gaudet earns world bronze in parallel slalom small final |website=[[CBC.ca]] |date=21 February 2023 |access-date=7 February 2026}}</ref>

During the final race of the [[2022–23 FIS Snowboard World Cup]], Obmann earned his first career [[FIS Snowboard World Cup|World Cup]] victory on 18 March 2023. With the win he earned 100 points, to defeat [[Maurizio Bormolini]] by four points in the overall rankings, and two points in the men's parallel  slalom.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fis-ski.com/snowboard-alpine/news/2022-23/ledecka-zogg-and-obmann-take-the-spoils-at-dramatic-season-s-end-slalom-in-berchtesgaden |title=Ledecka, Zogg and Obmann take the spoils at dramatic season’s end slalom in Berchtesgaden |website=fis-ski.com |date=18 March 2023 |access-date=7 February 2026}}</ref> The next day he won the mixed parallel event, along with [[Sabine Schöffmann]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fis-ski.com/snowboard-alpine/news/2022-23/obmann-and-schoeffmann-win-team-event-as-world-cup-season-wraps-up-in-berchtesgaden |title=Obmann and Schoeffmann win team event as World Cup season wraps up in Berchtesgaden |website=fis-ski.com |date=19 March 2023 |access-date=7 February 2026}}</ref>

In January 2026, he was selected to represent Austria at the [[2026 Winter Olympics]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.vol.at/this-is-austrias-squad-for-the-2026-winter-olympics/9947810 |title=This is Austria's Squad for the 2026 Winter Olympics |website=vol.at |date=26 January 2026 |access-date=7 February 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fis-ski.com/snowboard-alpine/news/2025-26/ones-to-watch-in-snowboard-alpine-at-the-milano-cortina-2026-winter-olympics |title=Ones to Watch in Snowboard Alpine at the Milano Cortina 2026 Winter Olympics |website=fis-ski.com |date=7 February 2026 |access-date=7 February 2026}}</ref>

