'''Hiroaki Nakabayashi''' ([[Japanese language|Japanese]]: 中林宏明; born September 5, 1988) better known as '''Bayashi''' or '''Bayashi TV,''' is a Japanese [[YouTuber]] and [[TikTok|TikToker]]. Known for his short-form [[mukbang]] and cooking videos, he has garnered a large following on social media with millions of followers across various platforms.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hoke |first=Carlie |date=2024-12-01 |title=Who Is The Man Behind Bayashi TV? |url=https://www.mashed.com/1720428/who-is-man-behind-bayashi-tv/ |access-date=2026-03-22 |website=Mashed |language=en-US}}</ref> He first joined YouTube in early January 2021 and TikTok in February 2020, uploading cooking tutorials and food [[ASMR]] videos on both.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Smith |first=Crawford |date=2022-12-08 |title=Japanese Food TikToker Bayashi On ASMR And The Joys Of Deep-Frying - Exclusive Interview |url=https://www.tastingtable.com/1129565/japanese-food-tiktoker-bayashi-on-asmr-and-the-joys-of-deep-frying-exclusive-interview/ |access-date=2026-03-22 |website=Tasting Table |language=en-US}}</ref>

== Career ==
Bayashi has seen a significant amount of [[Viral phenomenon|virality]] on social media across multiple platforms. In 2023, he uploaded a video with American food and body influencer [[Chef Rush]], which garnered over 900 million views as of 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Views: Bayashi TV Brings Us In, Behind the Cooking Counter |url=https://www.ahotset.com/web-series/the-views-bayashi-tv-brings-us-in-behind-the-cooking-counter |access-date=2026-03-22 |website=A Hot Set |language=en-US}}</ref>

