'''Judith Jáuregui''' is a Spanish classical pianist known for her interpretations and recordings of works by many composers, including Albéniz, Arriaga, Granados, Grieg, Falla, Bach, Beethoven, Chopin, Liszt, and Schumann. She has performed as a soloist on many top classical music stages, such as the [[National Auditorium of Music|Auditorio Nacional in Madrid]], the [[Palau de la Música Catalana|Palau de la Música]] in Barcelona, the [[Southbank Centre]] in London, the [[Louvre|Auditorium du Louvre]] in Paris, the [[Flagey Building|Flagey]] in Brussels, [[Konzerthaus Berlin|Konzerthaus]] in Berlin, [[Suntory Hall]] in Tokyo, [[National Centre for the Performing Arts (China)|NCPA]] in Beijing, Teatro Mayor in Bogotá, [[Schloss Elmau]] in Germany, and many more. She was born in [[San Sebastián]] (Basque Country) in 1985.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Moyano |first=Alberto |date=2024-04-17 |title=«Puedo decir que mi patria son las 88 teclas del piano» |url=https://www.diariovasco.com/culturas/musica/pianista-judith-jauregui-20240417182632-nt.html |access-date=2026-05-25 |website=El Diario Vasco |language=es}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Judith Jáuregui |url=https://franzschubertfilh.com/en/artistes/judith-jauregui/ |access-date=2026-05-25 |website=Franz Schubert Filharmonia |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Judith Jáuregui - —Chopin, Schubert, Schumann, Liszt, Mompou and Grieg |url=https://www.palaumusica.cat/en/judith-jauregui_1304085 |access-date=2026-05-25 |website=Palau de la Música Catalana |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Judith Jáuregui (Spain) |url=https://www.boesendorfer.com/en/artists/juidth-jauregui |access-date=2026-05-25 |website=Home |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Mantilla |first=Jesús Ruiz |date=2013-06-07 |title=La pasión de Judith Jáuregui |url=https://elpais.com/elpais/2013/06/07/eps/1370605906_692921.html |access-date=2026-05-25 |work=El País |language=es |issn=1134-6582}}</ref>

